```json
{
  "summary": "QUERY PLAN: grain = one row per distinct (product, perishable supply) pair. No aggregation, this is a filtered lookup. Join supplies (s) to order_items (oi) on shared key product_id to resolve the product's display name, then filter to s.is_perishable_supply = true. DISTINCT prevents fan-out duplication since order_items has multiple rows per product_id (one per order item). Outcome: Review SQL preview — this is an ad hoc filtered lookup, not an exact match for the certified top_products or food_vs_drink_revenue blocks (neither exposes supply/perishable data), so a review-required DQL artifact is prepared using the supplies and order_items relations and their product_id join key.",
  "sql": "SELECT DISTINCT oi.product_name AS product_name, s.supply_name AS supply_name FROM jaffle_shop.dev.supplies s JOIN jaffle_shop.dev.order_items oi ON s.product_id = oi.product_id WHERE s.is_perishable_supply = true ORDER BY oi.product_name LIMIT 100",
  "viz": "table",
  "outputs": ["product_name", "supply_name"],
  "dql": {
    "entity": "supplies",
    "dimensions": ["product_name", "supply_name"],
    "filters": ["is_perishable_supply = true"]
  }
}
```
